  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A metal is heated in a furnace where a sensor is kept above the metal surface to read the power radiated (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>) by the metal. The sensor has a scale that displays <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a constant. When the metal surface is at a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>487</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>,&nbsp;the sensor shows a value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Assume that the emissivity of the metallic surface remains constant. What is the value displayed by the sensor when the temperature of the metal surface is raised to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2767</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#963;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> where <math><mi>T</mi></math> is in kelvin<br /><math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#963;</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>487</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> .....(i)<br /><math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#963;</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2767</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> ......(ii)<br />(ii) - (i)<br /><math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3040</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>760</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>",
